# OBJECTIVE 6: MAKE REPORTS TRACEABLE AND USEFUL

Every report should make it possible to understand how its findings were generated and what happened afterward.

Preserve, as appropriate:

- Assessment identifier and creation timestamp.
- Room and image association.
- Model and provider information available from the real API.
- Schema and assessment-rule versions.
- Structured findings and evidence references.
- Review status and user corrections.
- Calculation inputs and resulting index, if applicable.
- Known limitations and errors.

Avoid storing unnecessary personal information or raw photos in debugging logs.

Ensure reports cannot accidentally combine information from two different assessments.

Make report generation robust to missing fields, malformed data, and deleted or inaccessible images.

Printing, exporting, opening, saving, editing, and revisiting reports should work as intended. If a capability is not implemented, either implement it properly or remove misleading controls.

Keep the output understandable to ordinary users rather than exposing unnecessary technical detail.

