# DEFINITION OF DONE

The task is not done merely because the interface looks better.

It is complete to the extent that the actual implementation demonstrates the following:

1. The primary workflow functions reliably.
2. Findings are structured, qualified, and tied to appropriate evidence.
3. Unsupported conclusions are not silently presented as facts.
4. Image annotations are validated and evaluated against reference examples where applicable.
5. Any score is transparent, deterministic, and appropriately limited in meaning.
6. User corrections have consistent behavior.
7. Errors are handled honestly and recoverably.
8. Reports preserve correct, traceable data.
9. Security and privacy statements match the implementation.
10. Critical tests and available build checks have been run.
11. Existing useful functionality remains intact.
12. Known limitations are documented accurately.

Not every advanced capability must be added if it does not serve the product. Technical excellence means solving the right problems correctly, not maximizing the number of components.

